/* DATA DESCRIPTION:
Citation:	Aksnes, Dag Lorents (2021): Surface photosynthetically active radiation (PAR) in Masfjorden 2010-2011, western Norway [dataset]. PANGAEA, https://doi.org/10.1594/PANGAEA.932308, 
	In: Aksnes, DL (2021): Light measurements in Masfjorden 2010-2011, western Norway [dataset bundled publication]. PANGAEA, https://doi.org/10.1594/PANGAEA.932328
Abstract:	Surface solar irradiance was measured to support a nearby (within 500 m) cabled acoustic observatory (Prihartato et al. 2015, Christiansen et al. 2021, Kaartvedt et al. 2021) to study the behavior of mesopelagic fishes in Masfjorden, western Norway. Surface irradiance in air (PAR, 400 - 700 nm) was recorded every 15 minutes in the period from December 13, 2010 to August 17, 2011.
Keyword(s):	Light; PAR; spectral irradiance; surface light; underwater light
Supplement to:	Christiansen, Svenja; Klevjer, Thor Aleksander; Røstad, Anders; Aksnes, Dag Lorents; Kaartvedt, Stein (2021): Flexible behaviour in a mesopelagic fish (Maurolicus muelleri). ICES Journal of Marine Science, fsab075, https://doi.org/10.1093/icesjms/fsab075
Related to:	Kaartvedt, Stein; Sobradillo Benguria, Beatriz; Klevjer, Thor Aleksander; Røstad, Anders (2021): Cabled acoustic observatory [dataset]. University of Oslo, Norway, https://doi.org/10.21335/NMDC-1243831716
Further details:	Prihartato, Perdana K; Aksnes, Dag Lorents; Kaartvedt, Stein (2015): Seasonal patterns in the nocturnal distribution and behavior of the mesopelagic fish Maurolicus muelleri at high latitudes. Marine Ecology Progress Series, 521, 189-200, https://doi.org/10.3354/meps11139
Project(s):	Sustainable Management of Mesopelagic Resources (SUMMER)
Funding:	Horizon 2020 of the European Commission (H2020) (URI: https://research-and-innovation.ec.europa.eu/funding/funding-opportunities/funding-programmes-and-open-calls/horizon-2020_en), grant/award no. 817806: Sustainable management of mesopelagic resources (URI: https://doi.org/10.3030/817806)
Coverage:	LATITUDE: 60.885556 * LONGITUDE: 5.461389
